a Page We apologize for the inconvenience... ...but your activity and behavior on this site made us think that you are a bot. Note: A number of things could be going on here. If you are attempting to access this site using an anonymous Private/Proxy network, please disable that and try accessing site again. Due to previously detected malicious behavior which originated from the network you're using, please request unblock to site. Incident ID: 2004b439-cxfy-4a27-b9d6-42f888696ca3 Please solve this CAPTCHA to request unblock to the website You reached this page when trying to access https://pollfinder.sos.state.mn.us/ from 172.56.232.242 on March 26 2026, 03:10:58 UTC"}, {"url": "https://voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "title": "voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "snippet": "Seed source captured for Arizona voting information. Live page fetch was unavailable during collection."}], "state_fips": "04", "state_name": "Arizona", "polling_hours": "Arizona polling locations are generally open from 6:00 AM to 7:00 PM local time on Election Day. Any voter in line by 7:00 PM is entitled to cast a ballot.", "id_requirements": "Arizona requires voters to show photo ID at the polls. Acceptable photo IDs include an Arizona driver's license, state-issued ID, tribal enrollment card with photo, or other government-issued photo ID showing name and address. Voters without photo ID may present two non-photo documents showing name and address (e.g., utility bill, bank statement, government document). Voters who cannot provide ID may cast a provisional ballot and must verify their identity with the county recorder within five business days.", "polling_place_url": "https://my.arizona.vote/WhereToVote.aspx?s=address", "vote_by_mail_info": "Arizona is an all-mail ballot state for most voters. Active early voters receive a ballot automatically before each election. Voters who are not on the Permanent Early Voting List (PEVL) may request an early ballot no later than 11 days before the election. Mail ballots must be received by election officials by 7:00 PM on Election Day to be counted; postmark alone is not sufficient. Voters may also return their mail ballot in person at any official drop box or voting location by 7:00 PM on Election Day.", "state_abbreviation": "AZ", "voter_registration_url": "https://www.usa.gov/register-to-vote"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T03:10:21.844Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.13788-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.19876-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.665642-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.665642-07
