ions.hawaii.gov/resources/county-election-divisions", "vote_by_mail_info": "Hawaii conducts elections entirely by mail. All registered voters are automatically mailed a ballot before each election. Voters may return their ballot by mail (must be postmarked by Election Day and received within 7 days after Election Day), deposited in an official drop box by 7:00 PM on Election Day, or returned in person at a voter service center by the close of polls on Election Day.", "state_abbreviation": "HI", "voter_registration_url": "https://www.usa.gov/register-to-vote"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T02:43:57.468Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.149655-07	2026-03-25 19:57:10.062673-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.530373-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.530373-07
