o cast their ballot. Hours may vary slightly by county, so voters should confirm with their local county election office.", "id_requirements": "Indiana requires voters to present a photo ID at the polls. Acceptable forms of ID include an Indiana driver's license, state-issued ID card, U.S. passport, or military ID. The ID must display the voter's name, photo, and an expiration date showing the ID is current or expired after the last general election. Voters without an acceptable photo ID may cast a provisional ballot and must provide proof of identification to the county election board by noon 10 days after the election for the ballot to be counted.", "polling_place_url": "https://indianavoters.in.gov", "vote_by_mail_info": "Indiana allows any registered voter to request an absentee ballot without needing an excuse. Voters must request an absentee ballot by mail no later than 11 days before the election. Completed mail ballots must be received by the county election board by noon on Election Day. Ballots may be returned by mail or delivered in person to the county election board.", "state_abbreviation": "IN", "voter_registration_url": "https://indianavoters.in.gov"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T03:10:21.844Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.151926-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.203996-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.677517-07	2026-03-25 20:12:57.677517-07
