e for the inconvenience... ...but your activity and behavior on this site made us think that you are a bot. Note: A number of things could be going on here. If you are attempting to access this site using an anonymous Private/Proxy network, please disable that and try accessing site again. Due to previously detected malicious behavior which originated from the network you're using, please request unblock to site. Incident ID: e563afc6-cxfy-43f2-afaa-6460181ca0ed Please solve this CAPTCHA to request unblock to the website You reached this page when trying to access https://pollfinder.sos.state.mn.us/ from 172.56.232.242 on March 26 2026, 02:51:10 UTC"}, {"url": "https://voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "title": "voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "snippet": "Seed source captured for Washington voting information. Live page fetch was unavailable during collection."}], "state_fips": "53", "state_name": "Washington", "polling_hours": "Washington conducts elections primarily by mail, so traditional polling places are limited. In-person voting centers and drop boxes are available and typically open from 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM on Election Day. Hours for early in-person voting at vote centers vary by county. Any voter in line by 8:00 PM on Election Day is entitled to vote.", "id_requirements": "Washington does not require voters to show photo ID at the polls for mail ballot return or in-person voting at vote centers. First-time voters who registered by mail and did not provide a driver's license number, state ID number, or last four digits of their Social Security number may be asked to provide a copy of an acceptable ID (such as a utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document showing name and address) when returning their ballot or voting in person.", "polling_place_url": "https://www.vote.org/polling-place-locator", "vote_by_mail_info": "Washington is an all-mail voting state. All registered voters are automatically sent a ballot by mail before each election. Ballots must be postmarked by Election Day (the first Tuesday after the first Monday in November) or returned to an official drop box or voting center by 8:00 PM on Election Day. Voters may also return ballots in person at any county drop box or voting center. There is no separate request process required since ballots are mailed automatically to all active registered voters.", "state_abbreviation": "WA", "voter_registration_url": "https://www.usa.gov/register-to-vote"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T02:43:57.468Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.181224-07	2026-03-25 19:57:10.045422-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.500411-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.500411-07
