hink that you are a bot. Note: A number of things could be going on here. If you are attempting to access this site using an anonymous Private/Proxy network, please disable that and try accessing site again. Due to previously detected malicious behavior which originated from the network you're using, please request unblock to site. Incident ID: c75c3969-cxfy-4e6c-88b5-be7cd1868c59 Please solve this CAPTCHA to request unblock to the website You reached this page when trying to access https://pollfinder.sos.state.mn.us/ from 172.56.232.242 on March 26 2026, 02:51:25 UTC"}, {"url": "https://voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "title": "voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "snippet": "Seed source captured for West Virginia voting information. Live page fetch was unavailable during collection."}], "state_fips": "54", "state_name": "West Virginia", "polling_hours": "West Virginia polling places are generally open from 6:30 AM to 7:30 PM local time on Election Day. Any voter in line by 7:30 PM is entitled to cast a ballot. Specific hours may vary slightly by county, so voters should confirm with their local county clerk.", "id_requirements": "West Virginia requires voters to show ID at the polls. Acceptable forms of photo ID include a WV driver's license, U.S. passport, military ID, or other government-issued photo ID. Voters who do not have an acceptable photo ID may cast a provisional ballot and must provide ID to the county clerk within two days after the election for the ballot to be counted. First-time voters who registered by mail and did not provide ID verification during registration may also be subject to additional ID requirements.", "polling_place_url": "https://apps.sos.wv.gov/Elections/voter/FindMyPollingPlace", "vote_by_mail_info": "West Virginia allows any registered voter to vote absentee by mail without needing an excuse. Voters must request an absentee ballot from their county clerk. For primary and general elections, absentee ballot applications must typically be received by the county clerk no later than 6 days before the election. Completed ballots must be received by the county clerk by 7:30 PM on Election Day; postmarks alone are not sufficient — the ballot must be physically received by the deadline. Ballots may be returned by mail or delivered in person to the county clerk's office.", "state_abbreviation": "WV", "voter_registration_url": "https://www.usa.gov/register-to-vote"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T02:43:57.468Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.181877-07	2026-03-25 19:57:10.046405-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.503788-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.503788-07
