bWYiOiI3ZjkwMDBmZDFmZGQ4MC0xNTljLTRlODctODE4OC05NzM0MDc5NDI1NjYxLTE3NzQ0OTMzMjA3NDcwLTAwMzVjYzBmYWY1NjZmYTg2ZGExMCIsInJkIjoibW4uZ292In0=", "title": "Radware Captcha Page", "snippet": "Radware Captcha Page We apologize for the inconvenience... ...but your activity and behavior on this site made us think that you are a bot. Note: A number of things could be going on here. If you are attempting to access this site using an anonymous Private/Proxy network, please disable that and try accessing site again. Due to previously detected malicious behavior which originated from the network you're using, please request unblock to site. Incident ID: 552bae32-cxfy-4bd0-a6bf-099cdba56b73 Please solve this CAPTCHA to request unblock to the website You reached this page when trying to access https://pollfinder.sos.state.mn.us/ from 172.56.232.242 on March 26 2026, 02:48:41 UTC"}, {"url": "https://voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "title": "voterlookup.elections.ny.gov", "snippet": "Seed source captured for Oregon voting information. Live page fetch was unavailable during collection."}], "state_fips": "41", "state_name": "Oregon", "polling_hours": "Oregon is an all-mail voting state and does not have traditional polling places with set hours. However, official ballot drop boxes and county elections offices are available for in-person ballot return. Drop boxes are generally accessible around the clock in the weeks leading up to Election Day and close at 8:00 PM on Election Day. Voters needing in-person assistance should contact their county elections office for specific hours.", "id_requirements": "Oregon does not require voters to show photo ID at a polling place because the state votes entirely by mail. First-time voters who registered by mail and did not provide a driver's license number, state ID number, or last four digits of their Social Security number may be required to provide a copy of an acceptable ID document with their ballot. Acceptable documents include a utility bill, bank statement, government check, paycheck, or other government document showing the voter's name and address.", "polling_place_url": "https://sos.oregon.gov/voting/Pages/drop-box-locator.aspx", "vote_by_mail_info": "Oregon conducts all elections entirely by mail. Every registered voter is automatically mailed a ballot approximately 2 weeks before Election Day. Voters do not need to request a ballot. Completed ballots must be returned by 8:00 PM on Election Day, either by mail (postmarked by Election Day) or dropped off at an official drop box or county elections office by the 8:00 PM closing time on Election Day. No postage is required to return a ballot by mail in Oregon.", "state_abbreviation": "OR", "voter_registration_url": "https://www.usa.gov/register-to-vote"}	written	\N	state_resources_2026-03-26T02:43:57.468Z	claude:claude-sonnet-4-6	state_resources_enrichment_v1	state_resources_v1	2026-03-25 19:13:27.167684-07	2026-03-25 19:57:09.587276-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.01187-07	2026-03-25 19:57:11.01187-07
